Personal Portfolio — Flask
==========================

1. Install Python 3.9+ if you haven't already.
2. Open a terminal in this folder.
3. (Recommended) Create a virtual environment:
       python -m venv venv
       venv\Scripts\activate          (Windows)
       source venv/bin/activate       (macOS / Linux)
4. Install Flask:
       pip install -r requirements.txt
5. Run the app:
       python app.py
6. Open http://127.0.0.1:5000 in your browser.

Make it yours
-------------
* Edit the PROFILE dictionary at the top of app.py (name, section, course,
  subject, motto, skills, email, phone, social links …).
* Drop your photo into static/images/ and name it  profile.jpg
  — it will automatically replace the initials avatar.

Routes
------
/                      Home
/profile               Profile
/contact               Contact (with message form)
/works                 toUpperCase
/works/area/circle     Area of a circle
/works/area/triangle   Area of a triangle
/works/linkedlist      Interactive linked list


Contact form: where do messages go?
-----------------------------------
* Every message is saved in a file called  messages.jsonl  (next to app.py).
  Open it any time to read them. Nothing is sent over email by default.
* To ALSO get each message in your inbox (Gmail):
    1. Turn on 2-Step Verification in your Google account, then create an
       "App Password" (Google Account > Security > App passwords).
    2. Set these before running the app. In PowerShell:
           $env:MAIL_USER = "you@gmail.com"
           $env:MAIL_PASS = "your-16-letter-app-password"
           python app.py
       (MAIL_TO is optional - use it to send to a different address.)
  The visitor's email is set as "Reply-To", so you can just hit Reply.
* Never type your password or app password into app.py or upload it to GitHub.
